        "Fetch strategy for an extern→intern run. `full` (default, unchanged behavior) fetches the entire source result set every run and hash-diffs it against stored SynchronizationContracts, including garbage-collecting target objects no longer present in the source (`deleteInvalidObjects`). `incremental` injects the stored `cursorWatermark` into the source request (via `{{ cursor }}` Twig templating on `sourceConfig.endpoint`/`sourceConfig.query`) so only records changed since the watermark are fetched, advances the watermark only after a complete, successful fetch, and NEVER runs `deleteInvalidObjects`: an incremental fetch is a filtered subset of the source, so a target's absence from one run is not evidence of source deletion. An absent value is treated as `full`. No migration needed for existing Synchronizations.": "Fetch strategy for an extern→intern run. `full` (default, unchanged behavior) fetches the entire source result set every run and hash-diffs it against stored SynchronizationContracts, including garbage-collecting target objects no longer present in the source (`deleteInvalidObjects`). `incremental` injects the stored `cursorWatermark` into the source request (via `{{ cursor }}` Twig templating on `sourceConfig.endpoint`/`sourceConfig.query`) so only records changed since the watermark are fetched, advances the watermark only after a complete, successful fetch, and NEVER runs `deleteInvalidObjects`: an incremental fetch is a filtered subset of the source, so a target's absence from one run is not evidence of source deletion. An absent value is treated as `full`. No migration needed for existing Synchronizations.",
