        "Source-specific configuration overrides. Notable recognised keys: `resultsPosition` (dot-path to the objects array in the response, or `_root`/`_object`); `format: \"jsonl\"`. The fetched (and, if gzip, decompressed) body is parsed as line-delimited JSON, one record per line, instead of whole-document JSON/XML. Pair with `resultsPosition: \"_root\"` since the parsed line array IS the records list; `paginationQuery` (field name/dot-path to bump per page, default `page`); `paginationIn: \"body\"` (default `\"query\"`). Substitutes the next page value into the source's static `configuration.body` JSON template at the `paginationQuery` dot-path instead of the query string, for POST-body sources (e.g. TED's v3 search) whose pagination cursor lives in the request body. `deletionRatioThreshold` (float 0.0-1.0, default 0.10). The maximum share of this synchronization's existing contracts that one cleanup pass may garbage-collect before the deletion-ratio guard aborts the pass (warning logged + SynchronizationDeletionGuardedEvent dispatched); override per synchronization for legitimately volatile sources, or supply the explicit `forceDeletion` run parameter for a one-off override. `cursorField` (dot-path to the comparable cursor value on a fetched record, e.g. `updatedAt`. Same dotted-path-lookup-with-throw convention as `idPosition`/`getOriginId`) and `cursorComparator` (`gt`|`gte`, informational. The engine always takes the maximum observed value). Read only when the synchronization's top-level `syncMode` is `incremental`, to compute the persisted `cursorWatermark` after each complete fetch.": "Source-specific configuration overrides. Notable recognised keys: `resultsPosition` (dot-path to the objects array in the response, or `_root`/`_object`); `format: \"jsonl\"`. The fetched (and, if gzip, decompressed) body is parsed as line-delimited JSON, one record per line, instead of whole-document JSON/XML. Pair with `resultsPosition: \"_root\"` since the parsed line array IS the records list; `paginationQuery` (field name/dot-path to bump per page, default `page`); `paginationIn: \"body\"` (default `\"query\"`). Substitutes the next page value into the source's static `configuration.body` JSON template at the `paginationQuery` dot-path instead of the query string, for POST-body sources (e.g. TED's v3 search) whose pagination cursor lives in the request body. `deletionRatioThreshold` (float 0.0-1.0, default 0.10). The maximum share of this synchronization's existing contracts that one cleanup pass may garbage-collect before the deletion-ratio guard aborts the pass (warning logged + SynchronizationDeletionGuardedEvent dispatched); override per synchronization for legitimately volatile sources, or supply the explicit `forceDeletion` run parameter for a one-off override. `cursorField` (dot-path to the comparable cursor value on a fetched record, e.g. `updatedAt`. Same dotted-path-lookup-with-throw convention as `idPosition`/`getOriginId`) and `cursorComparator` (`gt`|`gte`, informational. The engine always takes the maximum observed value). Read only when the synchronization's top-level `syncMode` is `incremental`, to compute the persisted `cursorWatermark` after each complete fetch.",
